<h2>The Record Start in Kansas City</h2>
<p>Kansas City signed Walker in March to a three-year deal worth up to $45 million, weeks after he was named Super Bowl LX MVP. He ran for 135 yards on 27 carries in Seattle's 29-13 win over New England, the first running back to win the award since Terrell Davis. The Chiefs needed him: they finished 25th in rushing in 2025 during a 6-11 season, and their third-leading rusher was Patrick Mahomes.</p>
<p>Five games in, here's where Walker stands:</p>
